  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c257e3c51f03491d96f52e1051c8f8d4",
      "statement": "Authorization is capability-based: open() computes the caller's effective role from the permission graph and returns either the full OverseerClientInterface or a restricted UseOverseerInterface that implements all of Overseer but throws Unauthorized for everything outside the use allowlist (default-deny), tipping a use collaborator to UI-only access.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L28-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4fe70bdca0b8cf7afd4794204889b6c05513eedb8af02e2013b57fa645df12e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ba18f09c2a14b2a911dd2c00d5e85a7",
      "statement": "Effective role is the maximum role reachable from the owner through valid edges, where each edge grants min(edge role, sharer's effective role) and the owner is the implicit build root; it is computed live by the fixed-point computeEffectiveRoles() and is never denormalized.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L111-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48332b7ca2e2eff7e08ba1f7e9753d44e8ffec2632dbbe01ece695908d2f5a23:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L69-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cdc73eda61fb73ca8bb36ac265cef26eae50f12d5302d301735a4f7232b3d316:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a590ef44b876467fa918d882c440e65f",
      "statement": "A share key is a 128-bit value carried in the URL's #share fragment; the server stores only its HMAC-SHA-256 hash with a fixed domain-separation constant, so a database leak exposes no valid keys.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L40-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aa42329d9d6fb8f7e7ea2d0c0e3746c3fd1553327b99a2c56921e65b61aa3512:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/sharing.ts#L48-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f7221e0066032176adbce30cb856b9431de720ee65a25e18389b7b6387c19dd1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8c4746439bba4eb8a3b70aa349c183fd",
      "statement": "Revocation is lazy: removing a collaborator severs only the edges granting them access stdin a revoked share link only sets a revoked flag, nothing cascades, and the graph is never destructively pruned so access is reversible by re-adding; users who lose their only path simply become unreachable at open() time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L85-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f6bf36f07b76a4e3ec5041d1818b607f22565e83210b39dc03d90dd8e773da3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/sharing.ts#L97-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66e658cdbdadf10d27afa3699b0582c44dda51905f0a546e5b59836d46dbc044:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3400b1fe34b14d859a7742fcf8675d7b",
      "statement": "Because authorization is only checked at open(), removeCollaborator/revokeShareLink proactively restart the Overseer DO via ctx.abort() whenever the change actually removed or downgraded someone, flushing the severed edge first and delaying ~100ms, forcing every client to reconnect and re-evaluate the changed graph.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L153-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cad80912d0be0e60f837e1cb021173258193d341b2436fd56fcc0bae81139aca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88428e0da7fa4993b9461b8dd6452d14",
      "statement": "The observer mechanism enforces that when a non-owner opens a gadget, each relevant gatekeeper verifies via Gatekeeper.addObserver() that the user's own connected account can directly observe everything the gadget has historically read through that gatekeeper, and this is re-verified on every open.",
      "evidence": [
